#usda 1.0
(
    """W3 K4(0) — season-off (flowerless) wrapper for Shrub/Rhododendron.usd.

    WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  `SEASONAL_SUBPRIMS` has stripped `/Root/Flowers` off every
    Rhododendron since the realism-v1 layer landed, by calling `SetActive(False)` on
    the referencing prim and then making that prim instanceable.  Measured with
    usd-core 26.8: **USD discards opinions on descendants of an instance**, so the
    shared prototype is composed from the reference alone and still carries
    `Flowers` — every `place_shrubs` bed with the default `SHRUB_ORNAMENT` pool has
    been rendering a full-bloom magenta scan (76.7 % magenta basecolor) in a library
    that declares itself season-neutral.  Same defect class as the leaf-off trap the
    red team caught on `build_tree(bare=)` (F1, `redteam_s0710_rebuild.md` §1.2);
    this is its shrub half, and it is the one that was actually live.

    Putting the `over` in a **wrapper layer** moves the opinion above the instance
    boundary: the wrapper composes normally, the scene references the wrapper, and
    every instance then shares one prototype that has no flowers.  Instancing is
    kept, which this project treats as mandatory for vegetation.

    Convention and licence follow `Gray_Birch_bare.usda` (scene04, commit 024a985):
    the file lives **outside** the gitignored `assets/vegetation/` tree, contains no
    asset content — one relative reference and one `over` — and is therefore
    trackable while the geometry it points at stays untracked and procured by
    `assets/download_vegetation.py`.

    `metersPerUnit` MUST match the referenced asset (measured 0.01 on all 17
    vegetation USDs).  Layer units are advisory in USD — a mismatch here would not
    rescale anything, it would only lie to `add_vegetation`'s unit probe.
    """
    defaultPrim = "Root"
    metersPerUnit = 0.01
    upAxis = "Z"
)

def Xform "Root" (
    prepend references = @../vegetation/Shrub/Rhododendron.usd@
)
{
    over "Flowers" (
        active = false
    )
    {
    }
}
